## §10 Parent-event alias stash


PoD's duel-launcher parents (the events that call
`configure_start_single_combat_effect`) routinely save custom scope
aliases like `scope:spirit`, `scope:my_rival`, `scope:scheme` that
their follow-up events read after combat resolves. Under vanilla's
duel chain those scopes propagate through the event graph. The
minigame's scripted-GUI execute boundary breaks that chain, so
`pod_combat_sc_stash_parent_aliases_effect` captures each alias as a
story var on the `POD_combat_sc_context` story at launch, and
`pod_combat.9999` rebuilds them as saved scopes before firing the
parent's follow-up.

The whitelist below was audited across every PoD caller of
`configure_start_single_combat_effect` as of v1.18.3.1 integration,
re-audited 2026-07-05 for reads DOWNSTREAM of the OUTPUT_EVENT (the
original pass only checked the follow-up event's own reads, which
missed the task-contract chains - completion runs one or two events
later), then swept in full the same day: every intercepted entry
point's downstream chain was walked and adversarially verified,
adding 23 character aliases, 4 object aliases, and a scope-VALUE
stash (numbers/booleans; flag-typed values still can't ride it).
Each row stashed as `alias_<name>` on the sc_context story.

